# =====================================================================
# Release V055 -- usp_Rerun_Failed_Jobs longest-path ordering fix
# =====================================================================
# usp_Rerun_Failed_Jobs sequenced downstream reruns by SHORTEST-path level (each job pinned
# at the first level it was reached, never bumped). A job reachable via a short path but that
# DEPENDS on a job reached via a longer path landed at the SAME level as its dependency and
# could run BEFORE it on the Step-3 tie-break. Real-world hit: SILVER_PATIENTS + SILVER_
# PRACTITIONERS both failed; the daily aggregate (reads Dim_Patients = level 2) tied with
# Fact_Practitioner_Diaries (level 2) and ran first -> Worked_Hours = 0 -> blank Chair
# Utilisation / Revenue per Clinical Hour. Fixed to LONGEST-path levels (max(prereq)+1).
#
# DEPLOY-only (idempotent DROP/CREATE proc). No data change; re-run the affected loads after.
# NB: to correct the CURRENT prod state, re-run the aggregate (or a full build-only) once --
# this release only fixes FUTURE targeted reruns.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V055__rerun_failed_jobs_longest_path.manifest -SkipTests
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY  Fabric\Audit.usp_Rerun_Failed_Jobs.StoredProcedure.sql

TEST
